<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 10.249 percent from 10.245 percent at the previous auction on August 19.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Feb 25, 1997 (Feb 18, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.249 percent (10.245)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 977.950 milion (773.325 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.003 billion (911.825 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.101-10.291 percent (9.999-10.269)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.101-10.600 percent (9.999-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 208 (84)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 215 (99)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
